two related PartnerBot improvements (2026-07-17):

  A. Readiness reports (morning/evening) keep AT MOST TWO messages per
     recipient -- one current morning slot, one current evening slot --
     retention is SLOT-based (period_kind + user_id), never date-based.
     Covers _pf_send_partner_report (partner_stat_bot.py) plus the existing
     edit-in-place correction/recheck mechanism (_pf_correct_partner_message).

  B2. A new, separate immediate PartnerBot notification when a reserve
     account activation actually commits (reserve_activation_events.status
     -> 'done'). Covers the new _rsvan_* pipeline (partner_stat_bot.py).

B1 (immediate replacement-completion notification) is NOT re-tested here --
it is already fully covered by the existing, unmodified
tools/manager_replacement_partner_notify_selftest.py (the _arn_* pipeline
required no code change for this task; this file only adds a couple of
cross-pipeline isolation checks between the _arn_* and _rsvan_* namespaces).

Techniques (same as every other tools/*_selftest.py in this project):
  - partner_stat_bot.py cannot be imported standalone (real telethon.
    TelegramClient at module scope; Telethon is not installed locally) --
    the functions under test are extracted via ast.parse + ast.unparse +
    exec() and run FOR REAL against a temporary SQLite DB (never
    db/data_tpilot.db).
  - storage.py IS importable -> ensure_reserve_tables and the real settings
    KV table are exercised for real.
  - Windows here has no tzdata package -- not needed by anything under test
    in this file (no Kyiv-time formatting is exercised here).

Never: real Telegram network, real proxy/provider network, real process
spawn/stop, production DB/runtime/session/log access.

    python tools\\partner_readiness_reserve_notify_selftest.py
